From 5b50be3e6dc85eb920610d6f1db6c14809f7180c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:29:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] script: add P2MR (BIP 360) witness v2 program
 validation

Implement the Pay-to-Merkle-Root spending rules of BIP 360 draft v0.12.1
(bips commit 620871a7a442e276a058b487cd8743775fb499a4) behind a new
SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR flag.

A P2MR output is a native SegWit output with witness version 2 and a
32-byte witness program holding the Merkle root of the script tree. There
is no internal public key and no taproot tweak, so every spend takes the
BIP 341 script path directly: the control block is 1 + 32*m bytes instead
of 33 + 32*m, the folded Merkle root is compared to the witness program as
is, and a leaf at depth zero succeeds without executing the script. The
last bit of the control byte is unused by P2MR and must be 1 for every
leaf version, which the new SCRIPT_ERR_P2MR_WRONG_CONTROL_PARITY reports.
Leaf version 0xc0 is executed under the BIP 342 rules and reuses the BIP
342 signature message unchanged, so PrecomputedTransactionData::Init
precomputes the BIP 341 data for P2MR spends too.

Without SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR the branch is skipped entirely, which keeps the
existing unknown witness program behaviour, including
SCRIPT_VERIFY_DISCOURAGE_UPGRADABLE_WITNESS_PROGRAM.

Activation uses a new buried deployment, DEPLOYMENT_P2MR, with the height
parameter P2MRHeight. It never activates on mainnet, testnet3, testnet4 or
the default signet; it activates at height 1 on a custom signet and at
height 0 on regtest, where -testactivationheight=p2mr@N overrides it.
GetBlockScriptFlags sets the flag from that height onwards.

Since witness v2 programs of 32 bytes are no longer unconstrained on
regtest, feature_taproot.py no longer asserts that they are spendable with
an arbitrary witness, and rpc_blockchain.py expects the extra script flag
and deployment.
